1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,096
Good evening from the OROS closing desk.

2
00:00:03,096 --> 00:00:08,978
This morning the system named no pick, so tonight there is nothing to grade.

3
00:00:08,978 --> 00:00:13,700
No setup, no trade, no loss — that is the discipline working.

4
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:18,619
Why we grade in public: a forecast that is never checked is just content.

5
00:00:18,619 --> 00:00:24,009
Every morning call gets an evening verdict, and both go in the permanent record.

6
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:29,628
On the day, the book is up 102 dollars.

7
00:00:29,628 --> 00:00:32,860
Dropbox (DBX) leads, +2.3 percent.

8
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:36,948
Amneal Pharmaceuticals (AMRX) lags at -0.8.

9
00:00:36,948 --> 00:00:42,081
The checklist is clear: nothing requires action today.

10
00:00:42,081 --> 00:00:45,564
On screen, the day's gainers and laggards inside the paper book.

11
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:54,762
And here is the book itself — the actual holdings, identical to this morning's emailed report.

12
00:00:54,762 --> 00:01:03,612
6 positions, led by Arch Capital Group, ticker ACGL, Dropbox, ticker DBX, Amneal Pharmaceuticals, ticker AMRX.

13
00:01:03,612 --> 00:01:14,553
Every line carries its share count, its entry, and its exit — because a position without a defined exit is not a position, it is a hope.

14
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:21,263
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

15
00:01:21,263 --> 00:01:23,675
Every morning OROS proposes.

16
00:01:23,675 --> 00:01:34,268
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

17
00:01:34,268 --> 00:01:38,230
Inside the book today: 4 positions up, 2 down.

18
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:40,556
Best, DBX at +2.30 percent.

19
00:01:40,556 --> 00:01:42,364
Worst, AMRX at -0.79.

20
00:01:42,364 --> 00:01:47,360
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

21
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:54,594
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -2.74% per trade over 1425 graded positions.

22
00:01:54,594 --> 00:02:01,657
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 50% position size.

23
00:02:01,657 --> 00:02:06,824
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

24
00:02:06,824 --> 00:02:19,227
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 153 names close the day in Stage 2; position size stays cut to 50% until the record earns it back.

25
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:23,222
Over to the sports desk.

26
00:02:23,222 --> 00:02:33,147
Day 104 of the race: three books, the same one hundred thousand simulated dollars, since July sixth.

27
00:02:33,147 --> 00:02:39,796
In first place, the live self-rebuilding book, in blue, at 108,473.

28
00:02:39,796 --> 00:02:47,538
Then the frozen first portfolio, the green line, 10.9 thousand back at 97,534.

29
00:02:47,538 --> 00:02:53,393
Then the index fund, in gray, 12.8 thousand back at 95,634.

30
00:02:53,393 --> 00:02:56,172
The race has no finish line.

31
00:02:56,172 --> 00:03:00,738
Same books, same dollars, back at it tomorrow.

32
00:03:00,738 --> 00:03:05,899
Every line starts the same day with the same dollar.

33
00:03:05,899 --> 00:03:07,884
Nothing is restated.

34
00:03:07,884 --> 00:03:16,754
On screen, three equity lines grown from the same starting dollar: the frozen first book, the live book, and the index fund.

35
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:25,800
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

36
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:28,037
Nothing here is financial advice.

37
00:03:28,037 --> 00:03:31,019
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
